{"title":"Career Roadmap · Baker / Pastry Chef","role":"Baker / Pastry Chef","summary":"A Baker/Pastry Chef specialises in producing breads, pastries, cakes, plated desserts, viennoiserie, confectionery and other baked products. The career combines food science, baking technique, recipe development, temperature control, ingredient functionality, presentation, costing and kitchen operations.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Culinary Science / Bakery & Confectionery"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Culinary Science / Bakery & Confectionery → Baker / Pastry Chef"},{"type":"p","text":"A Baker/Pastry Chef specialises in producing breads, pastries, cakes, plated desserts, viennoiserie, confectionery and other baked products. The career combines food science, baking technique, recipe development, temperature control, ingredient functionality, presentation, costing and kitchen operations."},{"type":"p","text":"This is a directly aligned career for B.Sc Culinary Science / Bakery & Confectionery. Practical kitchen competence, consistency, hygiene and a strong portfolio are more important for early employment than collecting academic certificates."},{"type":"h","text":"Career facts"},{"type":"table","header":["Item","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc Culinary Science / Bakery & Confectionery"}],[{"text":"Entry career"},{"text":"Baker / Pastry Chef"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Culinary Arts · Bakery · Pastry · Food Production"}],[{"text":"Strongest foundations"},{"text":"Baking science + pastry technique + food safety"}],[{"text":"Important practical skills"},{"text":"Doughs, fermentation, pastry, cakes, chocolate and decoration"}],[{"text":"Business skills"},{"text":"Costing, inventory, menu planning and production"}],[{"text":"Digital skills"},{"text":"Excel, POS, inventory and recipe-management systems"}],[{"text":"Long-term route"},{"text":"Commis Baker/Pastry → Demi Chef → Chef de Partie → Sous Chef → Executive Pastry Chef"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Direct alignment","text":"Yes."},{"type":"p","text":"Entry-level titles may include Commis Baker, Commis Pastry, Bakery Assistant, Pastry Assistant, Junior Baker or Pastry Cook. The title Baker/Pastry Chef generally becomes more appropriate after practical kitchen experience."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","What should I focus on?"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Master baking fundamentals, food safety, pastry techniques, production discipline and recipe costing."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in artisan bread, French pastry, chocolate, plated desserts, cake design or large-scale production."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress toward Chef de Partie, Sous Chef, Pastry Sous Chef or Bakery Production Manager."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Become Executive Pastry Chef, Head Baker, Culinary R&D Specialist, consultant or bakery entrepreneur."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Food science + kitchen fundamentals"},{"text":"University + practical lab"},{"text":"Basic baking portfolio"},{"text":"Foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Bread, cakes and cookies"},{"text":"Bakery lab + practice"},{"text":"15–20 documented products"},{"text":"Technique"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Pastry + laminated dough"},{"text":"Practical training"},{"text":"Croissant/danish portfolio"},{"text":"Pastry skills"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Chocolate + confectionery"},{"text":"Specialist workshops"},{"text":"Chocolate/confectionery collection"},{"text":"Specialisation"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Food safety + costing"}